WEBVTT

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:18.200
<i>Oh Yeah!
tsuyogatte tobinotte kaze ni natte</i>

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:18.200
<i>Oh Yeah!
Be strong, jump on, become the wind</i>

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:24.250
<i>oozora kidou wo koero</i>

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:24.250
<i>Pass the orbit beyond the sky</i>

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:41.020
<i>osaekirenai maenomeri na speed</i>

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:41.020
<i>Can't hold back this rushing speed</i>

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:46.020
<i>minareta machi ga diorama ni naru</i>

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:46.020
<i>A familiar town turns into a diorama</i>

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:51.230
<i>futoumei na sora tsukinukerunda</i>

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:51.230
<i>Burst through the unclear skies</i>

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:56.410
<i>nayami toka fuman toka futtobashite</i>

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:56.410
<i>Blow away your worries and discontent</i>

00:00:56.570 --> 00:01:01.830
<i>manual doori no tabi nanka irane</i>

00:00:56.570 --> 00:01:01.830
<i>Who needs a journey that's by the book</i>

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:07.620
<i>mayottemo furuetemo koudo agete</i>

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:07.620
<i>Even if you're lost or trembling,
Raise the altitude</i>

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:12.630
<i>Oh Yeah!
ikigatte shikujitte tachiagatte</i>

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:12.630
<i>Oh Yeah!
Show off, mess up, stand back up</i>

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:17.720
<i>kimi to mitsumeru michi naru chiheisen</i>

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:17.720
<i>The unknown horizon I watch with you</i>

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:22.600
<i>saa tsuyogatte tobinotte kaze ni natte</i>

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:22.600
<i>Now, be strong, jump on, become the wind</i>

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:28.400
<i>asu wo terasu taiyou
mejirushi ni shitesa</i>

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:28.400
<i>Use the sun
That lights tomorrow as a guide</i>

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:34.230
<i>tonde ike jiyuu na Glorious World</i>

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:34.230
<i>Fly off to the Glorious World of freedom</i>

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:42.410
<i>The mysterious world where Digimon live,
the Digital World.</i>

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:50.770
<i>Taichi Yagami and the Chosen Ones
with their partner Digimon</i>

00:01:50.770 --> 00:01:54.510
<i>head to a new stage in their adventure.</i>

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:04.120
<i>Meanwhile, in the real world,</i>

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:07.790
<i>large vessels everywhere fell
into an uncontrollable state.</i>

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:10.770
<i>The world was facing a major crisis.</i>

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:15.990
<i>The counterplan that Koshiro found was...</i>

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:20.880
I know!

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:21.800
This!

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:23.030
What?

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:38.300
BREAK THROUGH THE SEA MONSTER BARRICADE

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:46.810
Yum!

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:55.070
Cloud Continent is so small now...

00:02:56.360 --> 00:03:00.070
I'd never have guessed that
we were on a cloud all this time.

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:02.070
Did you know?

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:07.660
At that altitude,
even Peckmon can't reach it...

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:10.850
If we can no longer return,

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:13.710
we have no choice but to move forward.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:19.470
I wonder what kind of Digimon
are over here.

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:24.720
By the way, I wonder
where Eldoradimon's going.

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:26.220
Hm?

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.480
EBIDRAMON

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:39.570
SEADRAMON

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:42.530
It's Seadramon and Ebidramon!

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:23.490
Don't tell me...

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:32.500
Koshiro-kun, did you find something?

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:35.250
Yes, the ships' uncontrollable state...

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:39.400
may be solved without
having to defeat that swarm of Zurumon.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:40.250
What?!

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:45.570
<i>The source of the problem
is the infiltration of the AIS system</i>

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:49.850
<i>that uses GPS signals as the base
to locate ship positions.</i>

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:55.190
<i>In other words, there's a bug
in the ships' positional data.</i>

00:04:56.150 --> 00:05:01.750
If we can fix this positional data bug,
the uncontrollable state can be stopped!

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:04.590
But the GPS can't be used, right?

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:05.550
Look.

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:06.410
Huh?

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:12.950
It's true the networks that go through
the GPS are infected and unusable.

00:05:13.370 --> 00:05:18.270
However, if it's through
the GMDSS system installed aboard ships,

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:24.920
we can send data through the previously
used satellite network without using GPS.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:26.680
Um...

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:31.060
G, M, D, SS?

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:38.270
The GMDSS is the system that sends out
SOS signals when ships are in distress.

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:39.440
Ohh!

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:43.210
And that network is still safe.

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:44.070
Yes.

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:46.710
So, if it's a distress signal,

00:05:46.710 --> 00:05:50.720
it can even reach
uncontrollable ships without problems.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:56.330
And distress signals include
the positional data of ships.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:06:00.880
In short, if we send a distress signal
from a responsive ship...

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:05.400
Through the uninfected network,

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:09.260
the correct positional data
will reach the uncontrollable ships!

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:15.200
That way, the AIS with
the bugged positional data will be fixed,

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:18.000
and the ships might regain control!

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:21.020
But will that reach all ships worldwide?

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:23.210
No.

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:27.250
A distress signal will only reach
up to a certain distance.

00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:31.450
But if the ship that receives
the signal sends out the next one,

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:35.370
we might be able to relay
the signals all across the world.

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:38.890
That's a lot of ifs...

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:40.000
But...

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:42.290
we have no other choice!

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:49.470
WARUSEADRAMON

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:51.490
Waruseadramon!

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:54.260
A Digimon ate another Digimon and evolved!

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:00.640
Takeru!

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:01.900
Patamon!

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:06.860
Agumon Evolution!

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.870
Greymon!

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:27.920
Gabumon Evolution!

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:41.140
Garurumon!

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:50.610
Falcomon!

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:57.990
Jyuoken!

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:33.530
Waruseadramon's saying...
that there's food here!

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:35.280
Food?!

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:40.040
Something's coming!

00:08:54.170 --> 00:08:55.630
This Digimon was called!

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.350
MEGASEADRAMON

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:06.960
Megaseadramon!

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:09.900
Be careful, they're both Ultimate Digimon!

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:13.320
Yamato, take Takeru
and Patamon away from here!

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:41.720
<i>I found the perfect fishing boat
in Yokohama!</i>

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:45.810
<i>I'll borrow this ship's system
to send out a distress signal.</i>

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:49.730
This is a distress signal?

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:54.490
Yes, the signal should be reaching
this uncontrollable ship right now.

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:01.840
The system has recovered!

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:02.700
What?!

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:06.500
It's fixed?!

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:10.750
Yes. Now, if that ship
will just understand our plan...

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:13.940
A distress signal...

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:15.070
I see!

00:10:15.070 --> 00:10:17.940
Okay, send out a distress signal
from our ship too!

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:19.010
Roger!

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:24.870
They understood!

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:26.990
So this is what you meant!

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:29.350
Yes, what's important is after this.

00:10:40.030 --> 00:10:44.870
Before there's any more damage,
we must stop all uncontrollable ships!

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:47.370
But with this many...

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:55.440
So slow! Hurry up! C'mon!

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:57.170
Shh! Mimi-chan!

00:10:57.630 --> 00:10:58.380
Huh?

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:06.970
Please hurry...

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:51.140
Fox Fire!

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:11.580
Taichi!

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:13.750
Taichi-san!

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:01.960
Taichi!

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:17.440
Air Shot!

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:48.010
Yes! Now, all the systems
should be recovered!

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:56.040
<i>Sora, the Zurumon have started to move!</i>

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:57.020
What?!

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:04.030
We're chasing them now!

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:07.110
Where are they going?

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:08.970
Hmm...

00:14:08.970 --> 00:14:13.790
Oh! Maybe they're changing locations
to a new feeding ground?

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:15.430
Feeding ground?

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:17.980
Those guys eat data, right?

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:20.540
They went to find more data to eat.

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:22.540
<i>Koshiro-san!</i>

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:39.560
There's black sparks coming out of
where Zurumon were eating!

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:42.060
I'll look into it!

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:58.330
Huh? Oh...

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:01.020
I've lost sight of them!

00:15:01.020 --> 00:15:02.850
Sorry, Sora!

00:15:02.850 --> 00:15:04.350
Don't worry.

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:07.170
At least the ships are back in control.

00:15:07.590 --> 00:15:09.090
Exactly!

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:14.850
The sparks here are disappearing too.

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:18.620
Is it because Zurumon disappeared?

00:15:18.620 --> 00:15:20.890
Koshiro-kun, what do you think?

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:25.960
This black energy was
most likely sent to the Digital World,

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:28.880
just like the energy
we saw with Calamaramon.

00:15:28.880 --> 00:15:29.960
What?!

00:15:29.960 --> 00:15:33.220
Something is about to happen again
on the other side.

00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:34.890
The Digital World!

00:15:34.890 --> 00:15:38.890
Looks like we gotta go...
I'm worried about Taichi and Yamato too!

00:15:38.890 --> 00:15:43.880
Wait, how do we get back there by the way?

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:46.550
I'm being called.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:47.920
Huh?

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:21.770
Air Shot!

00:17:31.530 --> 00:17:32.940
Yay!

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:38.840
I'm exhausted...

00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:40.660
Good job, Agumon!

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:49.750
New enemies?

00:17:54.510 --> 00:17:55.900
Oh no...

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:58.090
This many were called?

00:18:02.600 --> 00:18:03.850
Taichi!

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:08.020
Taichi...

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:09.860
Huh?

00:18:19.110 --> 00:18:20.620
Zudomon!

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:23.040
Joe Senpai!

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:39.890
Here we go!

00:18:42.350 --> 00:18:43.720
It's Koshiro!

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:03.370
Excuse me!

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:44.660
Garudamon!

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:47.660
Shadow Wing!

00:20:04.090 --> 00:20:05.140
Taichi!

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:07.680
Everybody...

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:11.020
You guys came back!

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:15.190
Taichi.

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:31.830
<i>Breaking news.</i>

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:33.350
<i>Just earlier,</i>

00:20:33.350 --> 00:20:38.630
<i>the uncontrollable large vessels in
certain areas have all regained control.</i>

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:41.280
<i>With this recovery,</i>

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:45.220
<i>all U.S. aircrafts have withdrawn
from the Strait of Hormuz.</i>

00:20:45.760 --> 00:20:49.930
<i>It looks as though a military clash
has been avoided for the time being.</i>

00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:55.160
<i>However, the cause of this incident
is still unknown,</i>

00:20:55.160 --> 00:20:59.290
<i>and some claim it may be tied
to the recent global network failures.</i>

00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:02.280
<i>Governments worldwide
are now exercising caution.</i>

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:14.120
Hikari, why are you here?

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:19.920
I don't know, but I was called.

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:45.570
<i>Why do these held hands</i>

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:45.570
<i>naze ima kono te to te nigitte</i>

00:21:45.740 --> 00:21:48.240
<i>And the warmth exchanged</i>

00:21:45.740 --> 00:21:48.240
<i>tashikameta taion wo</i>

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:50.700
<i>Make me reminisce now</i>

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:50.700
<i>natsukashiku omou noka</i>

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:56.290
<i>Why an abyss dancing with endless rain</i>

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:56.290
<i>naze samidare no susabu shinen</i>

00:21:56.460 --> 00:21:58.790
<i>The gaze of that smile</i>

00:21:56.460 --> 00:21:58.790
<i>hohoenda sono shisen ni</i>

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:00.170
<i>Makes me want to cry</i>

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:00.170
<i>nakitaku naru</i>

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:03.090
<i>So call me with that voice</i>

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:03.090
<i>sono koe de boku wo yonde kure</i>

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:05.260
<i>This weakness I cannot tell others</i>

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:05.260
<i>dare ni ienu kono yowasa ga</i>

00:22:05.420 --> 00:22:08.340
<i>I realize is my pillar to stand firm</i>

00:22:05.420 --> 00:22:08.340
<i>tsuyoku tatsu tame no jiku dato omoishiru</i>

00:22:08.510 --> 00:22:10.640
<i>Difference is what makes me adore you</i>

00:22:08.510 --> 00:22:10.640
<i>chigau kara itooshiku naru</i>

00:22:10.800 --> 00:22:13.600
<i>I just want to understand you and me</i>

00:22:10.800 --> 00:22:13.600
<i>tada wakaritai kimi to boku wo</i>

00:22:13.770 --> 00:22:15.810
<i>Scars grow the more we live</i>

00:22:13.770 --> 00:22:15.810
<i>ikiru hodo kizu ga fuete iku</i>

00:22:15.980 --> 00:22:19.060
<i>But still we seek the reasons for us</i>

00:22:15.980 --> 00:22:19.060
<i>sore demo sagashiteiru bokura no wake wo</i>

00:22:19.230 --> 00:22:21.320
<i>Overlaying them makes us beautiful</i>

00:22:19.230 --> 00:22:21.320
<i>kasanete wa utsukushiku naru</i>

00:22:21.480 --> 00:22:25.240
<i>I want to know now, I want to cry out</i>

00:22:21.480 --> 00:22:25.240
<i>ima wakaritai sakebi dashitai</i>

00:22:31.620 --> 00:22:33.200
<i>The Digimon Encyclopedia!</i>

00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:35.370
<i>Zudomon.</i>

00:22:35.540 --> 00:22:37.790
<i>This Digimon super evolves from Ikkakumon.</i>

00:22:35.540 --> 00:22:37.790
LEVEL: ULTIMATE

00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:39.830
<i>The husky body is powerful!</i>

00:22:37.960 --> 00:22:39.830
TYPE: SEA ANIMAL

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:43.340
<i>The special move, Hammer Spark,
is shocking in power!</i>

00:22:40.000 --> 00:22:43.340
SPECIAL MOVE: HAMMER SPARK

00:22:43.670 --> 00:22:45.210
<i>Now, let's check this out!</i>

00:22:45.380 --> 00:22:48.680
<i>I hear Zudomon's shell is a trophy
won off other Digimon.</i>

00:22:48.840 --> 00:22:50.390
<i>Is there a stock of them?</i>

00:22:50.550 --> 00:22:53.510
<i>If so, maybe the shell is changed
depending on mood.</i>

00:22:53.680 --> 00:22:55.060
<i>I'll check next time.</i>

00:22:57.980 --> 00:23:00.060
<i>Which Digimon will it be next time?</i>

00:23:01.860 --> 00:23:06.070
<i>On a new continent with powerful Digimon
attacking one after another,</i>

00:23:06.240 --> 00:23:08.990
<i>the Chosen Ones' new adventure begins!</i>

00:23:09.150 --> 00:23:11.990
<i>Next time on Digimon Adventure:
"To the New Continent"</i>

00:23:12.160 --> 00:23:14.950
<i>The adventure continues to a new world.</i>
